{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thank you for reporting this, Hannah, and for not replying. You were right to be cautious. Please don't click any links, reply to the email, or forward it to colleagues. Leave it in your mailbox for now so our security team can examine it. Someone from the team will look into the sender and block it if needed. Your account is active and I found no signs that anything was entered, but please don't share your password with anyone by email or phone. If you've already clicked a link or entered your password anywhere, tell us right away.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-sec-06: user hannah.lee@brightline.example (user_id 12, Finance, Payroll Specialist, not VIP) reports an email from 'IT Support' asking for her password to finish account setup. User says she did not reply. Checks: account active, not blocked, failed_login_count 0, device BL-LT-0112. Quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so the message was not caught by spam filtering. Sender address and subject were not included in the ticket, so Tier 2 will need them from the user or the mailbox. Per KB-008 this is always escalated for review and possible blocking. Note for Tier 2: the account has must_change_password=true and password_last_set 2026-10-11. Confirm whether there is a legitimate onboarding or password-change workflow that could make the email look plausible, and check whether other users received the same message. No release, reset, or block actions were taken. Next step: recover the sender and subject, and check sign-in logs if there is any sign of credential exposure.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
